    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d640">

                <pb facs="0686" n="582" xml:id="pg582"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.01/111: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in El Salvador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">McCafferty</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-03-07T18:00:00-05:00">March 7, 1932—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>32. Department’s 31, February 27, 2 p.m. What are the developments in this matter
                    and what, if any, steps are being taken to put the Government of Salvador on a
                    basis where recognition can be extended to it consistently with the provisions
                    of the 1923 Treaty?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
